    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Thread support for the TLS layer used by libcurl.</para>
<para>Some TLS libraries require that you supply callback functions to deal with thread synchronization.</para>
<para>See <ulink url="https://curl.haxx.se/libcurl/c/threadsafe.html">https://curl.haxx.se/libcurl/c/threadsafe.html</ulink></para>
<para>You can deal with this yourself, or in the case that RESTinCurl support your TLS library, you can use this class.</para>
<para>Currently supported libraries:</para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Opeenssl (only required for OpenSSL &lt;= 1.0.2) define <computeroutput>RESTINCURL_WITH_OPENSSL_THREADS</computeroutput></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>The class is written so that you can use it in your code, and it will only do something when the appropriate define is set.</para>
<para>This class is only available when <computeroutput><ref refid="restincurl_8h_1afd0e7fa196a2032a330b69cab346b463" kindref="member">RESTINCURL_ENABLE_ASYNC</ref></computeroutput> is nonzero. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
